Test Case: identity_user_assigned_updated_with_vm_extension
================================================================================

Test marked as INVALID due to test extraction error

Initial Error (after fixing resource_group_name):
Error: Reference to undeclared resource
  on main.tf line 96, in resource "azurerm_virtual_machine_extension" "test":
   96:   virtual_machine_id   = azurerm_linux_virtual_machine.test.id
A managed resource "azurerm_linux_virtual_machine" "test" has not been declared in the root module.

Root Cause Analysis:
The test extraction incorrectly placed the VM extension in main.tf instead of azurerm.tf.

From the upstream test source (linux_virtual_machine_resource_identity_test.go lines 490-549),
the identityUserAssignedUpdatedWithVMExtension test includes:
1. Two user-assigned identities (lines 494-504)
2. The Linux VM resource (lines 506-539)
3. The VM extension (lines 541-547) that references the VM at line 543

During test extraction:
- CORRECT: The VM was extracted to azurerm.tf.bak
- INCORRECT: The two identities were placed in main.tf (lines 82-92) instead of azurerm.tf
- INCORRECT: The extension was placed in main.tf (lines 94-100) instead of azurerm.tf

Impact:
When the test switches from azurerm.tf to azapi.tf (renaming azurerm.tf to azurerm.tf.bak):
- The VM resource definition disappears from the configuration
- The extension in main.tf (line 96) still references "azurerm_linux_virtual_machine.test.id"
- This reference becomes invalid because the resource is no longer declared

Why This Cannot Be Fixed:
1. The test guide specifies main.tf is "Trusted, DO NOT MODIFY"
2. The extension should have been in azurerm.tf so it would move to azurerm.tf.bak during the switch
3. This is a structural test setup issue, not a module implementation problem
4. The similar test "identityUserAssignedWithVMExtension" is also marked as "invalid" in test_cases.md

Comparison with Similar Test:
The test "identity_user_assigned_with_vm_extension" (without "updated") has the same issue
and is marked as "invalid". This suggests VM extension tests have systematic extraction problems.

Attempted Fix:
Attempt 1: Added missing "resource_group_name" parameter - SUCCESS
Attempt 2: Cannot fix extension reference issue due to main.tf modification constraint

Conclusion:
This test case is INVALID due to incorrect test extraction. The VM extension and its
dependencies should have been extracted into azurerm.tf, not main.tf. This is not a
module implementation error but a test setup error that prevents proper migration testing.

Recommendation:
Re-extract this test case with the VM extension placed in azurerm.tf instead of main.tf,
or create an extension.tf file that can be renamed along with azurerm.tf during the test.
